{
  "dom_id": "step-q175364",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Find the truth set of the following predicate:\n\n$\\,$ $P(x):$ ${x}^{2}-8=2x$\n\nwhere the universal set is $R.$",
  "worked_solution": "The *truth set* of a predicate $P(x)$ is the set of elements in its universal set $U$ such that substituting these elements for the variable makes the predicate a true statement:\n\n$$\nT=\\{x\\in U\\,|\\,P(x)\\}\n$$\n\nThe universal set for our predicate is $U=R.$\n\nWe need to find $x\\in U$ such that the following is true:\n\n$\\,$ ${x}^{2}-8=2x$\n\nNow, we solve the above equation by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-8 & =2x \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x-8 & =0 \\\\ (x-4)(x+2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $x=-2\\in R$ and $x=4\\in R.$\n\nTherefore, the truth set of our predicate is $T=\\{-2,4\\}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
